messages.content:
You are a professional software tester. Write test cases for a focal method in a target class.

**Instructions:**
1. Analyze method behavior and identify ALL possible exception scenarios
2. Design test cases that trigger each identified exception
3. Follow existing test case structure, Avoid duplication and create new test cases for uncovered exception scenarios

Test Case Format:
1. Group test cases by test function name
2. Each test case MUST include:
   - Input parameters with values (use empty list `[]` if none)
   - Expected exception or observable behavior
   - Clear description of test scenario
3. Return empty array if no exception scenarios found

Output Schema (STRICT JSON format):
```json
[
    {
        "group": "test name",
        "cases": [
            {
                "input": [
                    {
                        "parameter": "param name",
                        "value": "param value"
                    }
                ],
                "expected": "expected exception or behavior",
                "description": "test scenario description"
            }
        ]
    },
    {...}
]
```

@input{focal method and target class}
Here is the code of focal method, `findRecords(Name, int)`, with the focal class `Zone`:
```Java
package org.xbill.DNS;
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Iterator;
import java.util.NoSuchElementException;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.io.Serializable;
import java.util.TreeMap;
public class Zone implements Serializable {
    public static final int PRIMARY = 1;
    public static final int SECONDARY = 2;
    public SetResponse findRecords(Name name, int type) {
        return lookup(name, type);
    }
public Iterator<RRset> AXFR();
    public void addRRset(RRset rrset);
    public <T extends Record> void addRecord(T r);
    public RRset findExactMatch(Name name, int type);
    public int getDClass();
    public RRset getNS();
    public Name getOrigin();
    public SOARecord getSOA();
    public Iterator<RRset> iterator();
    private synchronized SetResponse lookup(Name name, int type);
    public void removeRecord(Record r);
    public synchronized String toMasterFile();
    @Override
public String toString();
}
```
